# Byte-sensitive test fixtures: checked out verbatim on every platform.
#
# engine/src/crs_catalog.rs asserts the catalog's embedded EPSG:2056 definition is
# byte-identical to engine/tests/data/epsg2056.projjson (ADR-026 implementation note:
# "reuses ... verbatim", held true by test). The catalog stores newlines as \n escapes
# inside a JSON string (platform-stable); the .projjson has real newlines, so without
# this pin a CRLF-autocrlf checkout (e.g. windows-latest CI) materializes different
# bytes than the LF blob git stores, and the assert fails on \r alone. Pin LF at
# checkout so "byte-identical" means the same bytes everywhere.
*.projjson text eol=lf

# Same class, same failure shape: kernel::publish::ceilings `include_str!`s this file and
# publish::ceilings::tests::ceilings_json_bytes_are_pinned_by_content_hash pins its content hash
# literally. A windows-latest CI checkout materialized it as CRLF (autocrlf=true) while the git
# blob is LF, hashing to 6406980021ca… instead of the pinned fd746c843f22… (run 34190120091).
# Pin LF at checkout for the same reason the .projjson line above does.
renderer/bundle-viewer/ceilings.json text eol=lf
